Title: F1-M02 — The Silent Relay (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

> FADE IN:

INT. SIGNALS TENT - NIGHT

[[AMBIENCE: receiver static, a pencil scratching, rain on canvas]]
[[MUSIC: low, held tension]]

A field tablet and a hand-drawn sketch of the relay compound lie under a shaded lamp. CAPTAIN ELIAN and MIRA stand over it.

MIRA
(serious)
Three friendly patrols were redirected into the same kill zone. The orders came from our own relay frequency.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(neutral)
Our frequency, not our hands. The schedule from the junction camp proved the first attack was timed. This proves someone is still talking.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: west tree line start, service path through scrub, drainage channel along the south, fenced relay compound east, service yard and water tower north of the road]]

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(measured)
A forged message can move an army as surely as a tank. The relay compound is lightly staffed, but the alarm will bring reinforcements.

MIRA
(firm)
Take the service path. Disable the transmitter and leave the civilian technicians alive.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(short)
Two scouts, two engineers, four rifles. No base, no second team. Two sightings and the garrison comes down the north road.

MIRA
(dry)
And the technicians are the only people who can tell us what that mast actually is. Dead witnesses prove nothing.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(pointing at map)
The channel is sunk below the road. Nobody looks into it. That is your way out.

MIRA
(concerned)
The signal strength is wrong for a mast that size, Captain. Either the set is bigger than the photographs show, or it is not where the mast is.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

> FADE OUT.
